# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Source files diff as text, unconditionally.
#
# git decides whether a blob is binary by looking for a NUL byte in its first
# 8000, and for an image that heuristic is exactly right. For source it is a
# trap, and a positional one. `apps/web/src/keyboard/registry.ts` joined two
# Map-key halves with a NUL typed as a raw byte rather than the `\u0000`
# escape; it landed at offset 6891, inside the window, and a 76-line edit to a
# reviewed module reported as
#
#     apps/web/src/keyboard/registry.ts | Bin 14293 -> 16354 bytes
#
# in `git diff`, in `git blame`, in `git log -p`, and in every review view on
# GitHub. Formatting, lint, typecheck and 1019 tests were green on it — a NUL
# is valid UTF-8 and valid TypeScript inside a string literal, so nothing in
# the toolchain had an opinion.
#
# Two other files carry the same raw byte past byte 8000 and have diffed
# normally for months. That is the argument for this file rather than against
# it: whether the defect hides your work depends on how much text is above it,
# so a file that is fine today flips the next time someone adds a header.
#
# `pnpm check:text` is what stops the byte getting in. This is the other half,
# and the two must stay a pair for the reason `check:public` gives about
# `copyPublicDir: false`: a guard that can be bypassed by one careless commit
# should not be the only thing standing between a change and its reviewer.
# `diff` forces a textual diff regardless of content, so the worst case for a
# future NUL is a check failure with the diff still readable, rather than a
# silent one with it hidden.
#
# `text=auto` normalises line endings on the way in, so a checkout on Windows
# cannot commit CRLF that Prettier then fails on in CI for a reason the author
# cannot reproduce.
#
# Only extensions actually in the tree are listed. There is not one tracked
# binary in this repository today — no image, font or archive; Inter arrives
# through `@fontsource-variable/inter` and `UI Images/` is gitignored — so a
# blanket `* diff` would be true and would also quietly cover the first real
# image someone adds. Extensions are the narrower claim.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

* text=auto

*.ts   diff text
*.tsx  diff text
*.mjs  diff text
*.js   diff text
*.json diff text
*.css  diff text
*.html diff text
*.md   diff text
*.sql  diff text
*.yml  diff text
*.yaml diff text
